---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.mjs';
---

<Base title="Credits & sources" description="Who drew, wrote, mapped and built this.">
  <article class="frame">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Fine print</p>
        <h1>Credits &amp; sources</h1>
      </header>
      <dl class="specs">
        <dt>Book illustrations</dt>
        <dd>The pen-and-ink sketches from the book, the hand-drawn chart of Lostman’s River, and the drawings on the Sketchbook page are © {site.artist}. Used with permission; please do not reproduce without asking.</dd>
        <dt>Field-guide art</dt>
        <dd>
          The fish plates, portraits, critters, boats, tackle, place scenes, chapter spots and emblems were generated with OpenAI’s image tool from the author’s written visual brief, then reviewed and corrected by the author. They are illustrations inspired by the book, separate from Linda’s originals, and not surveyed or scientific references.
        </dd>
        <dt>Photograph</dt>
        <dd>The dedication photo is courtesy of the McKillop family.</dd>
        <dt>Cover</dt>
        <dd>The book cover is © the authors and appears here at thumbnail size.</dd>
        <dt>Text</dt>
        <dd>Chapter summaries, field notes, knot steps and glossary were written for this site. The novel itself is © John and Linda McKillop and is not reproduced here.</dd>
        <dt>Knots</dt>
        <dd>Knot diagrams are drafts. Tying steps follow the demonstrations at <a href="https://www.animatedknots.com" rel="noopener">Animated Knots</a>, which are linked from each knot; no artwork from that site is used.</dd>
        <dt>Map</dt>
        <dd>
          Map data © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors (ODbL). Rendered with <a href="https://leafletjs.com" rel="noopener">Leaflet</a>. Place positions are approximate and some locations are fictional.
        </dd>
        <dt>Natural history</dt>
        <dd>Species facts drawn from Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission and National Park Service public information. Always check <a href={site.fwcUrl} rel="noopener">current FWC rules</a>.</dd>
        <dt>Type</dt>
        <dd>Source Serif 4 and Caveat, both under the SIL Open Font License, self-hosted.</dd>
        <dt>Built with</dt>
        <dd>Astro, static files, no cookies, no trackers beyond cookieless page counts.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
